#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""
local_ui_agent.py - A fully local, privacy-aware GUI agent.

PIPELINE   observe -> detect PII -> plan -> validate -> (approve) -> execute -> verify

PERCEPTION (each module optional, degrades gracefully)
  * Screen capture ........ mss
  * OCR ................... pytesseract (local Tesseract binary)
  * Computer vision ....... OpenCV contour-based control/button detection
  * Face detection ........ OpenCV Haar cascade (ships with opencv, no download)
  * NER ................... spaCy local model (en_core_web_sm, pre-installed)
  * Regex PII ............. email, phone, Aadhaar (Verhoeff), PAN, cards (Luhn), IFSC, UPI, IP
  * Contextual PII ........ values sitting next to labels such as "Password", "OTP", "DOB"

PLANNING
  * "ollama" planner: local LLM on loopback (http://127.0.0.1:11434). The model only
    ever sees PII-MASKED element text and is told screen text is untrusted data.
  * "rule" planner: deterministic, no model, e.g.  --goal "click Settings; type 'hello' into Search"

SAFETY
  * Network guard: every non-loopback socket / DNS lookup raises. No cloud requests possible.
  * Validator: schema, known targets, on-screen bounds, minimum size, face regions,
    blocked hotkeys, dangerous typed text, step/rate limits.
  * Approval gate: irreversible/sensitive actions require explicit y/N from the user
    (default deny; EOF/timeout = deny). Annotated screenshot saved for review.
  * Audit log (JSONL) contains masked text only.

INSTALL (do this while online, once; the agent itself never goes online)
  pip install mss opencv-python numpy pytesseract pyautogui spacy
  python -m spacy download en_core_web_sm
  # + install the Tesseract OCR binary for your OS
  # optional LLM: install Ollama, `ollama pull llama3.1:8b` (or any local model)

USAGE
  python local_ui_agent.py --goal "click File; click Open" --planner rule --dry-run
  python local_ui_agent.py --goal "Open the settings page" --planner ollama --model llama3.1:8b
"""
